Approved on the owner's behalf by the delegated checkpoint review, 2026-09-30 (delegation: the owner, 2026-09-30: 'it reviews and approves for me then starts the next goal').
Identity note: the delegation's template names the owner; this file says "the owner" instead, because K27 and I5 forbid a personal name in any tracked file ("the checkpoint file reads 'Approved by the owner, <date>'") and goal 3's case-sensitive identity scan would fail on a file no goal may edit.
P1 approved (Option B: ESP32-S3 everywhere on ESP-IDF v6.1.x, W5500 wired with INT, PoE+ by a bought 802.3at splitter, native Wi-Fi for K91): fits K25, K37, K51 and devices' buy-the-module rule, and moves off v5.3 before its 2027-01-25 EOL; the upgrade lands in goal 6 with the safety scans re-run on the new version (§0.7), never before.
P2 approved (Option A: stereo LPCM from optical and ARC, CEC on a Linux theater hub): it equals the "If deferred" scope, needs no codec licence or custom board, and AC-3/eARC wait on the owner's TV answers (Needs item) and a bench measurement.
P3 deferred (the homelab PR for Option B' is drafted on a branch and not opened; the line reads PROPOSED): B' changes the security boundary and cabling of the owner's home network (a second server leg, filtering moved from OPNsense to the host firewall, a physical patch cable), which is the owner's to judge; the safer "If deferred" loses nothing before goal 7.
P4 deferred (the recommended $791.31 tier is filed as the Needs packet, marked "awaiting choice"): buying is the owner's alone (K4, K38); nothing is ordered and no goal depends on the purchase.
P5 approved (Option C: Lit 3 + esbuild, node --test + happy-dom): the recommendation is also its "If deferred" line, keeps the licence allowlist without an MPL-2.0 exception, and K43 declined neither option as final.
P6 approved (Option B: UPnP AV renderer in Rust inside chorus-server plus OpenHome services; Soloist the only sidecar): K57 asks for every legal open protocol; OpenHome is open, and nothing K60 excludes (librespot, AirPlay 2 receiver, Cast) is used.
P7 approved (Option C: Soloist slots in their own network namespaces on macvlan): it is the only option that keeps K66's instance per room, saved group and live group; the mDNS collision it rests on is a LEAD that goal 17 must re-verify before building (bridge if refuted), the macvlan network reaches the homelab only by a never-merged PR (K28), and the API key and builds stay the owner's Needs steps.
P8 approved (Option A: an assist_satellite per voice room in chorus's own integration): the recommendation is also its "If deferred" line and fits K61, K71 and K73.
P9 approved (Option A: Symphonia 0.6.1 under an MPL-2.0 ADR, libopus, dr_flac; AAC off): K26 as refined by K95 names MPL-2.0 Symphonia per P9, and AAC stays off under K60's strict bar.
P10 approved (stock cards only; MQTT off by default with an opt-in read-only publisher and no HA discovery): it matches the "If deferred" line and avoids duplicate entities beside the K61 integration.
P14 deferred (drafts on chorus branches only): the safer option; it keeps chorus out of a repo whose program is still running, matches devices goal 4's own reply on row chorus-1 ("no chorus work in devices' goals; drafts stay on chorus branches"), and no goal before 24 needs it; goal 27 re-checks devices.
I1-I16 and I18-I20 kept as written: each follows from its cited decisions and none relaxes a §3.1 guardrail or re-opens a Not chosen option.
I17 amended: goal 2 fixes every HIGH finding except A-9, A-10 and A-13, whose fixes are new capability (endpoint jitter buffer, I2S writer and servo; amp map and NVS provisioning; a firmware console and offsets series); goal 2 does their non-capability parts (e.g. A-9's counter rename) and assigns the rest in its table to the goals the audit names (A-9: 8; A-10: 8 and 9; A-13: 7 and 8), and goal 2's line C reads them as assigned. Reason: K20 puts fixes before new capability and K32 puts foundations first, so building endpoint playout in goal 2, ahead of protocol v2 and P1's toolchain move, would invert the order; the adversarial check found I17, the packet and goal-2 line C in conflict with the audit's own suggested goals.
Goal 1's shopkit scrub-list note (bare first name left out of shopkit's case-insensitive scan) kept: the full name, email and local part still guard shopkit.
Still the owner's (Needs, not approved here): the P4 purchase; the three TVs, the ESP32-S3 boards (read-only chip report), the room list and wiring, the rack's units and depth, the Soloist terms clause; the P3 decision and any homelab apply; the Spotify API key and Soloist builds. None blocks goal 2.
